Description: A reproducible frequentist Network Meta-Analysis (NMA)
    computational engine and research compendium evaluating multi-arm,
    multi-treatment trial evidence. Implements 12 sequential mathematical
    engines, graph-theoretical Laplacian synthesis via netmeta, local and global
    inconsistency diagnostics (node-splitting, NetHeat spectral decomposition),
    probabilistic rank simulation (10,000 Monte Carlo iterations), Minimal
    Clinically Important Difference (MCID) frontiers, and high-resolution
    publication exhibits (300 DPI) adhering strictly to PRISMA-NMA 2015 and
    Cochrane Handbook guidelines.
